scope: |
  Two INBOX reports from rozum. (1) `toint-on-a-char…` part A is ALREADY on main as 2315f2ecf (the
  reporter's branch content, landed under another sha) — the entry only needs routing; part B,
  `String.toList` on the v2 lane, is a real gap: the dispatcher has toList for list/Option/Set/Map/
  LazyList/ArrayBuffer and none for StrV, so the selection eta-expands. Measured: --v1 answers 2 /
  List(a, b) / 195, v2 now REFUSES loudly (it printed `<closure>` before this morning's fix).
  Fix mirrors charAt: CharV elements, which render as the char and carry the code point.
  (2) `toint-on-a-non-integer-diverges`: the Rust arm is `parse::<i64>().unwrap_or(0)` while run
  throws, so `"abc".toInt` is 0 on one lane and fatal on the other. run is the oracle; the Rust arm
  changes. WIDENED to v2/src/Runtime.scala before editing it.
